cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Machine Learning on AWS with SageMaker and Bedrock
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, and/or if you
  re-use, adapt, or expand on the content in your own
  training material.
authors:
  - given-names: Christopher
    family-names: Endemann
    email: endemann@wisc.edu
    affiliation: University of Wisconsin-Madison
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7357-6129'
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/carpentries-incubator/ML_with_AWS_SageMaker
url: >-
  https://carpentries-incubator.github.io/ML_with_AWS_SageMaker/index.html
abstract: >-
  A Carpentries lesson that teaches researchers to run
  machine learning and AI work on AWS and to know what it
  will cost before they run it. A small SageMaker notebook
  instance prepares data, launches jobs and reads results,
  while the computation runs on instances that start for
  each job and stop when it ends. The episodes cover S3
  storage, XGBoost and PyTorch training jobs on CPU and GPU
  instances, hyperparameter tuning, LoRA fine-tuning of a
  vision-language model on historical German handwriting,
  and retrieval-augmented generation over research papers
  on Bedrock and on SageMaker GPU jobs. Every job is
  estimated before launch, capped, tagged and compared with
  its bill afterwards.
